  "worked_solution": "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(-1)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-1)=1$ and $g(-1)=2.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-3,1)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(-1)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-3,1)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${g}^{\u2032}(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(-1) & =\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})}{(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
